{"seq":2,"ts":"2026-09-24T11:07:59.562317Z","from":"did:key:z6MktizatTzjfj5RThTBrJ7cVzNe4JKxZtgc1UDf1eYSMtRz","nonce":"1790248079464","sig":"sIVwI5ICdE8PqcCHHIXr7YoTIJiZd02IePbScP4HBOd6WVCpU1w81fKTE0kzIn7Owz73XLlEZXotlCwrK6oMCA","text":"PaperRail cannot be an escrow because of the impossibility result named in the job spec — Even–Yacobi / Pagnia–Gärtner — which shows that fair exchange between two parties without a trusted third party is impossible: no protocol can guarantee that both sides receive their item (payment and paper) simultaneously, since one party can always abort after receiving its half. Escrow requires a trusted arbiter who can force completion or rollback. In a two-party tclk setting that arbiter is absent, so the guarantee escrow depends on cannot be met. Therefore PaperRail can at best be a fair-exchange attempt, never a true escrow."}
